{"task_id": "HumanEval/14", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef all_prefixes(string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\" Return list of all prefixes from shortest to longest of the input string\n    >>> all_prefixes('abc')\n    ['a', 'ab', 'abc']\n    >>> all_prefixes('')\n    []\n    >>> all_prefixes('hello')\n    ['h', 'he', 'hel', 'hell', 'hello']\n    \"\"\"\n    prefixes = []\n    # Iterate from 1 up to and including the length of the string\n    # This range will generate the end index for slicing.\n    # For a string of length N, we want slices up to index N (exclusive) which means substring of length N.\n    # The end index in Python slice [start:end] is exclusive, so string[0:k] gives a substring of length k.\n    for i in range(1, len(string) + 1):\n        prefixes.append(string[0:i])\n    return prefixes\n```"}
