{"task_id": "HumanEval/70", "solution": "```python\nimport collections\n\ndef strange_sort_list(numbers: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    if not numbers:\n        return []\n\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n    num_deque = collections.deque(sorted_numbers)\n    result = []\n    is_min_turn = True\n\n    while num_deque:\n        if is_min_turn:\n            result.append(num_deque.popleft())\n        else:\n            result.append(num_deque.pop())\n        is_min_turn = not is_min_turn\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\n\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    '''\n    Given the lengths of the three sides of a triangle. Return the area of\n    the triangle rounded to 2 decimal points if the three sides form a valid triangle.\n    Otherwise return -1\n    Three sides make a valid triangle when the sum of any two sides is greater\n    than the third side.\n    Example:\n    triangle_area(3, 4, 5) == 6.00\n    triangle_area(1, 2, 10) == -1\n    '''\n    # Check if the sides can form a valid triangle\n    # 1. All sides must be positive\n    if a <= 0 or b <= 0 or c <= 0:\n        return -1\n    # 2. The sum of any two sides must be greater than the third side\n    if not (a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1\n\n    # If it's a valid triangle, calculate the area using Heron's formula\n\n    # Calculate the semi-perimeter\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2\n\n    # Calculate the area\n    # Note: The expression inside sqrt might be very slightly negative due to floating point\n    # inaccuracies for degenerate triangles (e.g., (3,4,7)). Taking max(0, ...) handles this\n    # to avoid math.sqrt(negative_number) error, though for strictly valid triangles\n    # where sum of two sides > third side, this shouldn't be an issue.\n    # However, for sides like (2, 3, 5), which is degenerate, the condition a+b>c fails,\n    # so we return -1.\n    area = math.sqrt(s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c))\n\n    # Round the area to 2 decimal points\n    return round(area, 2)\n```"}
