{"task_id": "HumanEval/75", "solution": "```python\ndef is_multiply_prime(a: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is the multiplication of exactly 3 prime numbers.\n    The number 'a' is less than 100.\n\n    Args:\n        a: An integer less than 100.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if 'a' is the multiplication of 3 prime numbers, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a < 8 or a >= 100:\n        return False\n\n    prime_factors_count = 0\n    temp_a = a\n\n    divisor = 2\n    while divisor * divisor <= temp_a:\n        while temp_a % divisor == 0:\n            prime_factors_count += 1\n            temp_a //= divisor\n            if prime_factors_count > 3:\n                return False\n        divisor += 1\n\n    if temp_a > 1:\n        prime_factors_count += 1\n\n    return prime_factors_count == 3\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/76", "solution": "```python\ndef is_simple_power(x, n):\n    if n == 1:\n        return x == 1\n\n    if x == 1:\n        return True\n    \n    if x <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    temp_x = x\n    while temp_x > 1:\n        if temp_x % n != 0:\n            return False\n        temp_x //= n\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/77", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef iscube(a: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer 'a' is a cube of some integer number.\n\n    Args:\n        a: An integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if 'a' is a perfect cube, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0:\n        return True\n\n    abs_a = abs(a)\n    cbrt_approx = round(pow(abs_a, 1/3))\n\n    for i in range(max(0, cbrt_approx - 2), cbrt_approx + 3):\n        if i * i * i == abs_a:\n            return True\n    \n    return False\n```"}
