_grades"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/82", "solution": "```python\ndef is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Helper function to check if a number is prime.\n    A prime number is a natural number greater than 1 that has no positive\n    divisors other than 1 and itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n <= 3:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n    \n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n    return True\n\ndef prime_length(string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Write a function that takes a string and returns True if the string\n    length is a prime number or False otherwise.\n\n    Examples:\n    prime_length('Hello') == True  # Length is 5, which is prime\n    prime_length('abcdcba') == True # Length is 7, which is prime\n    prime_length('kittens') == True # Length is 7, which is prime\n    prime_length('orange') == False # Length is 6, which is not prime\n    \"\"\"\n    length = len(string)\n    return is_prime(length)\n```"}
