{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "```python\ndef anti_shuffle(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Processes the input string `s` word by word, sorting the characters within each\n    word based on their ASCII values, while preserving the original positions\n    and order of spaces.\n\n    Args:\n        s: The input string.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new string with characters within each word sorted alphabetically\n        (by ASCII value).\n\n    Examples:\n        anti_shuffle('Hi') == 'Hi'\n        anti_shuffle('hello') == 'ehllo'\n        anti_shuffle('Hello World!!!') == 'Hello !!!Wdlor'\n    \"\"\"\n    processed_parts = []\n    current_word = \"\"\n\n    for char in s:\n        if char == ' ':\n            if current_word:\n                sorted_word_chars = sorted(list(current_word))\n                processed_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted_word_chars))\n                current_word = \"\"\n            processed_parts.append(char)\n        else:\n            current_word += char\n\n    if current_word:\n        sorted_word_chars = sorted(list(current_word))\n        processed_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted_word_chars))\n\n    return \"\".join(processed_parts)\n```"}
