{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef sort_array(array: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of non-negative integers based on the parity of the sum\n    of its first and last elements.\n\n    Args:\n        array: A list of non-negative integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list, which is a sorted copy of the input `array`.\n        The original `array` is not modified.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) <= 1:\n        return array[:]\n\n    first_element = array[0]\n    last_element = array[-1]\n\n    sum_first_last = first_element + last_element\n\n    sort_descending = (sum_first_last % 2 == 0)\n\n    return sorted(array, reverse=sort_descending)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "```python\ndef encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Encrypts a string by rotating each lowercase English letter four places forward in the alphabet.\n\n    The rotation shifts letters 'down' (forward) by two multiplied by two places,\n    resulting in a 4-place shift. For example, 'a' becomes 'e', 'b' becomes 'f'.\n    The alphabet wraps around, so 'w' becomes 'a', 'x' becomes 'b', and so on.\n    Non-alphabetic characters are left unchanged.\n\n    Args:\n        s (str): The input string to be encrypted.\n\n    Returns:\n        str: The encrypted string.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> encrypt('hi')\n        'lm'\n        >>> encrypt('asdfghjkl')\n        'ewhjklnop'\n        >>> encrypt('gf')\n        'kj'\n        >>> encrypt('et')\n        'ix'\n        >>> encrypt('Hello, World!')\n        'Lipps, Asvph!' # Example demonstrating non-alphabetic characters and uppercase handling\n    \"\"\"\n    encrypted_chars = []\n    SHIFT = 4\n\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            offset = ord(char) - ord('a')\n            new_offset = (offset + SHIFT) % 26\n            encrypted_char = chr(ord('a') + new_offset)\n            encrypted_chars.append(encrypted_char)\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            offset = ord(char) - ord('A')\n            new_offset = (offset + SHIFT) % 26\n            encrypted_char = chr(ord('A') + new_offset)\n            encrypted_chars.append(encrypted_char)\n        else:\n            encrypted_chars.append(char)\n\n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)\n```"}
